## The design discipline
Ordinary infrastructure is designed by load and span; its register state is
whatever the materials happen to give. Pulse-designed infrastructure is
specified by (mass, bulk density) FIRST through the Pulse Chip, so each
article's state fate - SPENT, PENDING, or NONE - is CHOSEN at the drawing
board and its full transition ledger is printed before any fabrication
door opens. The seat is a dial: bulk density alone moves the split at
1/4 ln(rho ratio). All figures below are computed in-run
(pulse_infra_run.json); none are hand-carried.

## The three design windows (computed from the filed edges)
- SHELL-HOLD (SPENT class): bulk 500.1 to 15,483.9 kg/m3 - inside
  the shell with no pending pulse at either wall.
- PENDING-ENTRY: bulk 342.6 to 500.1 kg/m3 - below the floor,
  inside the clock's remaining step (ln rho_inf = 0.09453); the crossing
  position on the remaining clock is set by where in the window the
  density sits.
- PENDING-EXIT: bulk 15,483.9 to 22,604.3 kg/m3 - inside the
  shell, out through the ceiling before the terminal state (the
  tungsten/gold/platinum class of seats; specified knowingly or not at all).
- GAP-HOLD (NONE class): at or below 342.6 - no crossing at any epoch.

